IPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast and axilla  is a modified radical mastectomy specimen consisting of a left breast  25 x 23 x 7cm  and overlying skin ellipse 20 x 8cm  and axillary tissue 6 x 6 x 1 5cm  The specimen is inked black and serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm ill defined  firm white nodule which comes to 2 5cm from the closest deep margin  Just inferior to the mass is a 5 x 4 x 3cm fibrotic firm area with cystic change which is about 1 5cm from the closest deep margin  A D  the firm nodule  E H  fibrotic area with cystic change I  the closest deep margin J L  axillary lymph nodes Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  additional left axillary node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm aggregate of adipose tissue which is dissected to reveal 2 lymph nodes measuring REMOVED_DATE to 1 2cm in the greatest dimension  The two lymph nodes are submitted in toto as cassette M  Resident  AQING CHEN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  LYMPH NODES  ADDITIONAL LEFT AXILLA  EXCISION   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  30 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  30 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 06 CLINICAL DATA  Rule out breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  100    MODERATE TO POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  EXTENDING TO MULTIPLE INKED RESECTION MARGINS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor measures approximately 1 8cm in greatest dimension by gross examination  No definite vascular invasion is identified  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 35                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 07 34 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm portion of pink tan fibrofatty breast tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal pink and white  shiny  semifirm cut surface  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  1  and saved frozen  The remaining tissue is submitted entirely in A through B  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST LEFT BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  EXTENDING TO THE MARGINS  O R  Resident  SCOTT D  URBAN  HMS O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
