hology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  12 AUG 03 at 16 00 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  A  right axillary node  are 2 pieces of fatty tissue with lymph nodes that measure REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  The lymph nodes are bisected and submitted separately in cassettes A B  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  B  right simple mastectomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm simple mastectomy with overlying skin measuring REMOVED_DATE x 10 0cm  The nipple areola region measures REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm  There are no scars on the skin  A stitch designates 12 o clock on the specimen  The surgical margins are inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  The deep margin of the specimen is smooth and does not contain any visible skeletal muscle  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a mass that measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm  This mass is located 0 4cm from the posterior margin and 2 0cm from the anterior margin  The cut surface of the mass is tan white with areas of hemorrhage  Although the mass has an irregular shape  the borders are fairly well defined  No axillary lymph nodes are identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  C F  Mass with nearest posterior margin  G H  Fibrous tissue away from mass  Resident  TRACY L  DAVIS  MD   Ph D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION PART B  B