Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery Unit Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  KEVIN S  HUGHES  M D  Resident  Matthew M Johnson  M D  Frozen Section Pathologist  Andrew E Rosenberg  MD Frozen Section Consultant s   Melinda J Lerwill  M D  Frozen Section Resident  James E  Davis  M D  Signed Out by  Joshua Kish  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  Left breast mass  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  1  INVASIVE CARCINOMA  2 2 CM  WITH ADENOSQUAMOUS AND SPINDLE FEATURES  FOCALLY POSITIVE AT A TISSUE MARGIN  2  HEALING BIOPSY SITE   SEE NOTE   NOTE  This is an unusual carcinoma that consists of a relatively well circumscribed nodule of malignant cells with focal squamous differentiation and malignant spindle cells with a moderate mitotic rate  Focally  the spindle cells merge with the carcinoma cells supporting a histologic relationship  Immunohistochemical stains for heavy chain myosin  calponin  p63  and cytokeratin highlight the lack of myoepithelial cells around many of the glands as well as single epithelial cells  Stains for cytokeratin 903  wide spectrum keratin  and epithelial membrane antigen also highlight the single cells  The case has been reviewed with Drs  Sgroi  Koerner  and Lerwill who agree with the above interpretation  The results of immunohistochemical staining for estrogen receptor  progesterone receptor  and Her2 neu protein expression and of fluorescence in situ hybridization studies for Her2 neu gene amplification will be reported in an addendum  BREAST  LEFT  MEDIAL FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  LEFT  CEPHALAD FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST