Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  05 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  05 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 11 30 CLINICAL DATA  Abnormal mammogram                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  90    GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO MULTIPLE INKED SURFACES  SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  10    CRIBRIFORM AND COMEDO TYPES  EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  AND PRESENT AT INKED SURFACES  NOTE  NO BLOOD AND LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION IS SEEN  ESTROGEN AND PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR STAINS WILL BE PERFORMED ON FORMALIN FIXED TISSUE  THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 17 22                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 10 36 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm lumpectomy specimen  inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm ill defined stellate pink tan mass abutting multiple resection margins  Representative sections are frozen as FX 1  and resubmitted in A  Representative sections in B J  Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   INFILTRATING DUCTAL AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Timothy R  Quinn  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST   report_end  , Checked.
