ures in 10 high powered fields  The morphologic findings are compatible with the patient s reported history of metastatic poorly differentiated carcinoma of the breast  The results of immunohistochemical staining for estrogen receptor  progesterone receptor  and Her2 neu protein expression and of fluorescence in situ hybridization studies for Her2 neu gene amplification are pending on slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and will be reported in an addendum  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right breast lumpectomy   are 2 fragments of unoriented fibroadipose tissue that measure REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  respectively  Each fragment is inked black  The largest fragment is serially sectioned to reveal a white firm cut surface with no distinct mass or lesion grossly appreciated  The first fragment is serially sectioned from one end to the other to reveal firm white tissue with no masses or lesions grossly appreciated  The entire specimens are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire large fragment sequentially submitted from one end to the other   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire smaller fragment  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right axillary nodes   are multiple fragments of fibroadipose tissue that aggregate to 8 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 1cm  Multiple candidate lymph nodes are identified ranging in greatest dimension from REMOVED_DATE to 2 2cm  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   5 candidate lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 candidate lymph node bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Largest lymph node bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Section of fibroadipose tissue with possible candidate lymph nodes  Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on Wednesday REMOVED_MONTH 25   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 01 55 35PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Fi