d and entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   medial final shaved margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm portion of fibroadipose tissue which is unoriented  The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  skin over mass  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm ellipse of tan unremarkable skin which is unoriented  The surgical margin is inked entirely in black  and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a fibrotic dermis and grossly unremarkable subcutis  The specimen is entirely submitted with the ends in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and the body in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Aliyah Rahemtullah M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Aliyah Rahemtullah M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Review by Melinda J Lerwill M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by Atul K Bhan M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION PART C  BREAST  RIGHT FINAL SUPER