Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  11 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 16 10 CLINICAL DATA  History of poorly differentiated  infiltrative ductal carcinoma on a prior incisional biopsy of a left breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     A  BREAST  LEFT   LUMPECTOMY  1  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SOLID TYPE  MULTIPLE FOCI  SEE NOTE  2  MICROCALCIFICATIONS  3 MULTIPLE INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMAS  4 FOREIGN BODY GRANT CELL REACTION  FAT NECROSIS  AND SCAR TISSUE  CONSISTENT WITH OLD BIOPSY CAVITY  B  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLARY  DISSECTION  FIVE LYMPH NODES ARE NEGATIVE FOR TUMOR  NOTE  The resection margins are free of tumor  No infiltrating ductal carcinoma is seen in the lumpectomy specimen  Diagnosis by  Leonard Atkins  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 02                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name and unit number  in two separate parts  Labeled  left breast mass  suture posterior margin  is a 11 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm breast lumpectomy specimen with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm skin ellipse that contains a linear  centrally located  3 3cm well healed scar  There is a suture in place designating the posterior surface  The specimen is oriented with the skin ellipse placed at the anterior  5 o clock position  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm white tan  firm  stellate lesion  with a central 0 1cm cystic cavity  that is located 0 6cm from the deep margin  0 4cm from the anterior surface  0 6cm from the lateral margin  1 5cm from the medial margin  5 5cm from the superior margin  and 0 6cm from the inferior margin  Surrounding the breast mass are a few focal areas of fat necrosis as well as some punctate