ly sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 8cm fairly well circumscribed stellate gray white mass  which comes to within 0 9cm from the posterior and anterior margins and abuts the anteroinferior margin  There are no other masses or lesions grossly identified  The remaining parenchyma is approximately 10  dense white fibrous tissue and the remaining tan yellow lobulated adipose tissue  Representative sections are submitted as follows  E  Tumor to anterior margin  F  Tumor to posterior margin  G  Tumor to anteroinferior margin  H  Tumor to superior margin  I  Tumor  J  Fibrous tissue lateral to tumor  K  Fibrous tissue medial to tumor  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional subareolar tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm aggregate of fibrofatty breast tissue fragments which are submitted in toto in cassette L  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  subdermal nodules  are two REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm tan yellow tissue fragment which are submitted in toto as M  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margin  superior half of cavity  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm aggregate of fibrofatty partially cauterized breast tissue fragments  The specimen is serially sectioned to display a cut surface consisting of approximately 10  dense white fibrous tissue and the remaining a tan yellow adipose tissue  There are no masses grossly identified  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes N V  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margin  inferior half of cavity  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm aggregate of fibrofatty breast tissue fragments which are serially sectioned to reveal a cut surface consisting of approximately 10  dense white fibrous tissue and the remaining a tan yellow lobulated adipose tissue  There are no distinct masses or lesions grossly identified  The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in cassettes W DD  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  non sentinel nodes  axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm aggregate of tan yellow lymph node bearing adipose tissue fragments  There are multiple lymph nodes dissected out ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  The lymph nodes are entirely submitted as follows  EE  5 whole lymph nodes  FF  4 whole lymph nodes  GG  2 whole lymph nodes  HH LL  1 bisected lymph node each  MM NN  Largest lymph node serially sectioned and entirely submitted  Gross Description by  JAMES BARRY Resident  TAI YUAN LIN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  SENTINEL NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY   POSITIVE FOR CARCINOMA  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  SENTINEL NODE  2  RIGHT AXILLARY   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN ONE HALF  O R  Resident  JULIE ANN NAGLE  MD O R  Diagnosis by  SELIM NASSER  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL LYMPH NODE PART B  RIGHT BREAST  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART C  ADDITIONAL SUBAREOLAR TISSUE EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART D  SUBDERMAL NODULES  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART E  BREAST  RIGHT  SUPERIOR HALF OF CAVITY  FINAL SHAV PART F  BREAST  RIGHT  INFERIOR HALF OF CAVITY  FINAL SHAV PART G  RIGHT AXILLARY NON SENTINEL LYMPH NODES , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  24 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  24 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 10 14 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY     INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  MODERATELY TO POORLY DIFFERENTIATED   GRADE 2 3 3   90   WITH FOCAL VENOUS INVASION BY TUMOR  THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED     INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  SOLID TYPE  10   FOCALLY PRESENT AT THE INKED RESECTION MARGIN  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 17 57                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  31 MAY 95 at 08 19 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm portion of yellow to red fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a pale white to tan firm nodule  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm  within 0 1cm of the closest inked resection margin  representative section of the nodule frozen as frozen section  1  now A with the remaining tissue entirely in B through K  Resident  Timothy R  Quinn  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT BREAST  CARCINOMA WITH NECROSIS AND INFILTRATION  O R  Resident  SCOTT D  URBAN  HMS O R  Diagnosis by  Max L  Goodman  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
