 tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  The tumor cell membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells  Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  Show strong  3   over overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  Immunohistochemistry to assess vascular invasion Focal lymphatic invasion is present  It is best seen on deeper sections immunostained for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and Factor VIII  the results of which support the presence of lymphatic invasion  rather than blood vessel invasion   The initial focus interpreted as vascular invasion is no longer present on the deeper sections  although a focus of ductal carcinoma in situ  supported by a p63 immunostain  is present in the same region  raising the possibility that the focus in fact represents ductal carcinoma in situ with retraction artifact  Nevertheless  lymphatic invasion is present elsewhere in the core biopsy  Addendum  2 by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  3  RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Not Amplified   See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  97  to chromosome 17 signals  97  in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  Results at or near the cutoff point  ranging from REMOVED_DATE   2 2  should be interpreted with caution  Addendum  3 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSY  report_end  , Unchecked.
