nters are Bcl 2 negative and Bcl 6 positive   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  is negative  but may be technically suboptimal  T cells   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  positive  are in a normal interfollicular distribution  The nodular meshwork of the follicular dendritic cells is  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  positive  Ki67 shows a high proliferative rate with polarization in the reactive follicles  Kappa and lambda light chains by in situ hybridization show normal polyclonal plasma cells  Overall  the morphological and immunohistochemical findings are consistent with a reactive peritumoral process  Dr  N L  Harris reviewed the slides and concurs with the interpretation  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL ANTERO SUPERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE 3  WITH FOCAL NECROSIS  BOTH INVOLVING 1 OF 4 TISSUE BLOCKS AND PRESENT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE INKED RESECTION MARGIN IN ONE FOCUS  SEE NOTE   2  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  Immunostains for keratin  calponin  myosin  and p63 support the diagnosis of invasive ductal carcinoma and ductal carcinoma in situ  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL LATERAL MARGIN   EXCISION  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE 3  WITH COMEDONECROSIS  INVOLVING 2 OF 3 TISSUE BLOCKS AND PRESENT REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE INKED RESECTION MARGIN IN ONE FOCUS  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL MEDIAL MARGIN   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE   NOTE  The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically evaluated  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL INFERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE   NOTE  The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically evaluated  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL DEEP MARGIN   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE   NOTE  Multiple levels examined  The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically evaluated  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL ANTERO INFERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE 