ve value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 24 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of breast which is inked and sectioned to reveal a tan  firm area containing an ill defined firm nodule  0 6cm in greatest dimension  The remainder of the specimen is composed of fatty tissue  No frozen done  The entire specimen is submitted in A through J  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  which is inked and sectioned to reveal dense  fibrotic cut surface  which is mixed with areas of adipose tissue and breast parenchyma  No discrete lesion is identified  No frozen section is done  The majority   90   of the specimen is submitted in K through T  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  FIBROUS AREAS AND 0 6CM NODULE SUGGESTIVE OF FIBROADENOMA  NO LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE TUMOR IDENTIFIED  GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  NO AREA SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING TUMOR SEEN  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  HENRY DONG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Frederick William Ackroyd  M D  Eugene Francis Ruffolo  M D  PART