inomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  03 AUG 98 at 15 58 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm fatty breast with a 7 x 0 8cm skin ellipse  and orienting sutures  The triple suture represents the nipple margin  The double suture represents the deep margin and the single suture represents the superior margin  The entire specimen is inked in black  the superior border is overinked in yellow  the posterior deep portion is overinked in blue and the  nipple margin  is overinked in orange  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral posterior surface to reveal a 0 6cm tan firm area approximately 0 5cm from deep nipple margin  and a 1 0cm hemorrhagic area near the superior aspect of the specimen  SECTION CODE A B  0 6cm tan firm area  C D  Superior 1 0cm hemorrhagic area  E G  Other areas of breast parenchyma  H  Skin  I  Medial resection margin  J  Lateral resection margin  Gross Description by  JEROME T  O CONNELL JR   MD Resident  GUILLERMO J TEARNEY  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  LESION TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  ZUOQIN TANG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  HOWARD CHANG  MD O R  Staff Pathologist  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Hugh Auchincloss Jr   M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Unchecked.
